                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>All measured parameters are within normal limits except for a mildly elevated chloride level. This isolated mild hyperchloremia may be clinically insignificant but could suggest mild dehydration, renal tubular acidosis, or compensation for metabolic acidosis. Correlation with clinical context and other laboratory findings is recommended. No acute abnormalities detected.</td>
